TITLE:: NdefRackHintBar
summary:: a strip that says what the mouse is over, and folds away
categories:: Libraries>NdefRack
related:: Classes/NdefRackGUI, Classes/NdefRackModuleView

DESCRIPTION::
The same idea as the hint bars in the module family, ParaEQ and SuperDirtGUI,
written here so this extension keeps depending on nothing: a line along the
bottom of a window that describes whatever the pointer is on, so a rack full of
small controls and ports can be read without a manual. The rack window has one;
this is how to give another window the same.

code::
(
var w = Window("hints", Rect(200, 200, 340, 120));
var hints = NdefRackHintBar();
var b = Button().states_([["press"]]);
var k = Knob();
w.layout = VLayout(HLayout(b, k), HLayout(nil, hints.toggle), hints.view);
hints.attach(b, "a button that does nothing");
hints.attach(k, { "the knob is at %".format(k.value.round(0.01)) });
hints.watch(w);
w.front;
)
::

A hint is a String, or a Function answering one. The Function is called with
the view and the pointer's x and y, which is what a view drawing several things
needs - a module in the rack is one UserView with many controls in it. Moving onto
nothing in particular puts the bar back to its default, link::#-note:: changes
that default, and link::#-toggle:: is a checkbox that folds the bar away.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: defaultString
what the bar says when the pointer is over nothing.
ARGUMENT:: height
22 unless given.

METHOD:: defaultHeight
22.


INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: view
The bar, to put in a layout.

METHOD:: watch
Let the window report the mouse over its views - without it no hint arrives -
and put the bar back to its default over the gaps between them. Once, after the
window exists.

METHOD:: attach
Give views a hint.
ARGUMENT:: views
a view, or an Array of them.
ARGUMENT:: hint
a String, or a Function called with the view, x and y.
RETURNS:: views, so a control can be wrapped where it is built.

METHOD:: note
Change what the bar falls back to, and show it now - how the rack says what the
last copy, paste or delete did.

METHOD:: string
What the bar says now.

METHOD:: clear
Back to the default.

METHOD:: toggle
A checkbox that folds the bar away and brings it back; the same one every time.
It has to sit outside the bar.

METHOD:: visible
Whether the bar is shown. Kept here rather than asked of the view, which answers
false until its window is shown.

METHOD:: defaultString
What the bar says over nothing.
